  {'id':'d263_105','subject':'english-communication','question':'Which sentence correctly uses the comparative degree?','options':['This mango is more sweeter than that.','This mango is sweeter than that.','This mango is most sweet.','This mango is the more sweet.'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Sweeter is the comparative form of sweet. Do not use more with one-syllable adjectives — more sweeter is a double comparative.','difficulty':'medium'},
