  {'id':'d263_188','subject':'english-communication','question':'Which sentence uses its vs its correctly (belonging to the crop)?','options':['The crop has lost it\'s color.','The crop has lost its color.','It\'s color has faded.','The crop lost it\'s leaves.'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Its (no apostrophe) is a possessive pronoun. It\'s = it is. The crop has lost its color (belonging to the crop) is correct.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d263_189','subject':'english-communication','question':'ASSERTION-REASON: Assertion (A): Idioms should be used sparingly in technical agricultural writing. Reason (R): Technical writing aims for precision and clarity; idioms can be ambiguous, especially for non-native speakers.','options':['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A','A is true but R is false','A is false but R is true'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Technical writing requires precise, unambiguous language. R correctly explains why idioms (which carry figurative meaning) should be avoided.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d263_190','subject':'english-communication','question':'The word versatile as used in Rice is a versatile crop means:','options':['Difficult to grow','Adapted to a wide range of uses','Expensive to market','Sensitive to climate'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Versatile means able to adapt to many functions or conditions. Rice is versatile because it is used in many food products.','difficulty':'easy'},
  {'id':'d263_191','subject':'english-communication','question':'The correct question tag for Let us go to the demonstration plot is:','options':['won\'t we','don\'t we','shall we','will we'],'correct':2,'explanation':'For sentences starting with Let us, the question tag is shall we? Example: Let us go, shall we?','difficulty':'hard'},
  {'id':'d263_192','subject':'english-communication','question':'Which sentence demonstrates correct parallel structure?','options':['She likes farming, to garden, and weeding.','She likes to farm, to garden, and to weed.','She likes farming, gardening, and to weed.','She likes to farm, gardening, and weed.'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Parallelism requires consistent grammatical form. She likes to farm, to garden, and to weed (all infinitives) is correctly parallel.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d263_193','subject':'english-communication','question':'The term agronomy refers to:','options':['Study of farm animals','Science of soil management and crop production','Study of plant diseases','Forest science'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Agronomy is the science and technology of producing and using plants for food, fuel, and land management — focusing on soil management and crop production.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d263_194','subject':'english-communication','question':'ASSERTION-REASON: Assertion (A): A curriculum vitae (CV) is longer and more detailed than a resume. Reason (R): A CV includes complete academic and professional history, while a resume is a brief summary.','options':['Both A and R are true and R is the correct explanation of A','Both A and R are true but R is NOT the correct explanation of A','A is true but R is false','A is false but R is true'],'correct':0,'explanation':'Both statements are true. R correctly explains why a CV is longer — it provides complete academic and career details.','difficulty':'medium'},
  {'id':'d263_195','subject':'english-communication','question':'Which sentence has a misplaced modifier?','options':['The farmer used a sharp sickle.','I saw a bird watching from the window.','She planted seeds carefully.','He harvested the golden wheat.'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Watching from the window appears to modify bird — a misplaced modifier. It should be: Watching from the window, I saw a bird.','difficulty':'hard'},
  {'id':'d263_196','subject':'english-communication','question':'What is précis writing?','options':['Expanding a passage into a longer version','Summarizing a passage in one-third its length','Translating a passage into another language','Copying a passage verbatim'],'correct':1,'explanation':'Precis writing is the art of summarizing a passage into about one-third of its original length while retaining all key ideas.','difficulty':'medium'},
